  "body": "What happens: PR #2138 changed the rapid law: a lateral rapid at or above the clearance plane is now re-read against the program ahead, and a traverse through stock under the stock top is convicted (Warning::RapidInStock). A project saved before that change carries cached verdicts made under the old law. The post gate counts only the WARN records that ride the stream from the cache. It does not re-run the rapid law. The stamp digest did not change, so an old cache still reads fresh. The user opens the project, posts without generating, and gets G-code that traverses rapids through uncut stock with no warning.\n\nExpected: a change to a verdict law marks cached verdicts stale. Two known mechanisms: a project-version migration (the v29 -> v30 line in project/apply.rs did exactly this for the sweep_hit alphabet: \"a cached verdict from the old laws re-derives stale\"), or a salt bump of the op stamp (stamp.rs writes b\"camcraft-op-stamp-v2\").\n\nEvidence: posting.rs line 501: \"Cached generation warnings ride the stream as WARN records, so the engine's own warning count is the gate.\" The gate in program_ops checks tool, spindle law, and OpStatus only. No path at post time re-runs verify::rapids (grep over posting.rs, posting_per_op.rs, program_entry.rs: no verify call). e7050be17 (the fix of #2121) touches neither project/ nor the stamp salt.\n\nFound while reviewing #2138 (lane review comment 6911362655, non-blocking note).\n\nDone means: one mechanism is chosen and shipped; a test posts a document whose cache holds a pre-law \"clear\" verdict for a traverse-through-stock path, and the post refuses with a named regenerate instruction.\n",
